#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setup {#setup}"
msgstr "Einrichtung {#setup}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The helper module [`mpo_learning.jl`](https://github.com/Qiskit/documentation/blob/main/docs/tutorials/assets/classical-shadows/julia/mpo_learning.jl), which the Setup cell downloads, implements the learner. The tutorial calls the following functions from it:\n"
msgstr "Das Hilfsmodul [`mpo_learning.jl`](https://github.com/Qiskit/documentation/blob/main/docs/tutorials/assets/classical-shadows/julia/mpo_learning.jl), das die Einrichtungszelle herunterlädt, implementiert den Lernalgorithmus. Das Tutorial ruft daraus die folgenden Funktionen auf:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Function | Purpose |\n"
"| --- | --- |\n"
"| `kicked_ising_reference(N, D; depolarization)` | Exact MPO of the ideal kicked-Ising state, or of the state after local depolarizing noise |\n"
"| `split_settings(group; seed, train_fraction)` | Randomly assign measurement settings to training and testing sets (half each by default) |\n"
"| `training_marginals(train; ell, prior)` | Shadow estimates of every learning window, from the training settings only |\n"
"| `fitted_prior(ideal, train)` | Prior for common randomized measurements (CRM), fitted to the measured purity of each window, as in the paper |\n"
"| `learn_mpo(marginals, N; ell, maxbond, sweeps)` | Sweep the one-site update of the paper along the chain, starting from the maximally mixed state |\n"
"| `max_fidelity(a, b)`, `mpo_overlap(a, b)` | Exact $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}$ and $\\mathrm{tr}(ab)$ between two MPOs |\n"
"| `afc_estimate`, `afc_statistics`, `afc_prefix_curve` | AFC estimates of $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}$ and $S_2$ from the testing settings, with jackknife error bars |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Funktion | Zweck |\n"
"| --- | --- |\n"
"| `kicked_ising_reference(N, D; depolarization)` | Exakter MPO des idealen Kicked-Ising-Zustands oder des Zustands nach lokalem depolarisierendem Rauschen |\n"
"| `split_settings(group; seed, train_fraction)` | Messeinstellungen zufällig Trainings- und Testmengen zuweisen (standardmäßig je zur Hälfte) |\n"
"| `training_marginals(train; ell, prior)` | Shadow-Schätzungen jedes Lernfensters, nur aus den Trainingseinstellungen |\n"
"| `fitted_prior(ideal, train)` | Prior für gemeinsame randomisierte Messungen (CRM), angepasst an die gemessene Reinheit jedes Fensters, wie im Paper |\n"
"| `learn_mpo(marginals, N; ell, maxbond, sweeps)` | Das Ein-Site-Update des Papers entlang der Kette durchlaufen, beginnend mit dem maximal gemischten Zustand |\n"
"| `max_fidelity(a, b)`, `mpo_overlap(a, b)` | Exaktes $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}$ und $\\mathrm{tr}(ab)$ zwischen zwei MPOs |\n"
"| `afc_estimate`, `afc_statistics`, `afc_prefix_curve` | AFC-Schätzungen von $\\mathcal{F}_{\\max}$ und $S_2$ aus den Testeinstellungen, mit Jackknife-Fehlerbalken |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-19
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The learner stores the MPO in the Pauli basis. This keeps the model Hermitian with unit trace, but it does not force the model to be positive semidefinite, so the notebook reports how negative its eigenvalues become.\n"
msgstr "Der Lernalgorithmus speichert den MPO in der Pauli-Basis. Dadurch bleibt das Modell hermitesch mit Spur eins, aber es erzwingt nicht, dass das Modell positiv semidefinit ist, weshalb das Notebook berichtet, wie negativ seine Eigenwerte werden.\n"

